# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every value here is either required in production
# or an explicit override; nothing in this file is a secret that must stay out of
# a deploy except SHOPIFY_API_SECRET.


# ── Database (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# MongoDB, read by prisma/schema.prisma. It holds live Shopify access tokens, so
# losing it logs out every merchant and makes every webhook fail HMAC.
#
# The database name after the host is REQUIRED — Prisma's MongoDB connector has
# no default database, and omitting it fails at connect time rather than at
# generate time, surfacing as a 500 on the first query instead of a build error.
#
# Use a separate database name for dev and production against the same cluster,
# or a separate cluster. Never point a dev deploy at the production database: the
# session collection is the merchants' logged-in state.
#
#   DATABASE_URL="mongodb+srv://USER:PASS@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/viewer3d?retryWrites=true&w=majority"
#
# Atlas also requires the deploy's egress IP in the project's Network Access
# allowlist. A blocked IP surfaces as a connect timeout on the first query, which
# looks exactly like a bad password.
DATABASE_URL=


# ── Shopify (required in production) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `shopify app dev` injects all four itself from the linked app and rotates
# SHOPIFY_APP_URL on every tunnel, so leave them unset locally — a stale value
# here silently wins over the CLI's and breaks OAuth. Set them only where the
# CLI is not the thing running the process.
#
# SHOPIFY_API_KEY=
# SHOPIFY_API_SECRET=
# SHOPIFY_APP_URL=https://your-app-domain.example.com
# SCOPES=write_products,write_files,write_themes,read_locales


# ── Billing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Creates app subscriptions as *test* charges: the merchant is shown the normal
# approval screen and is never billed. Development stores only.
#
# Leave this UNSET everywhere else. Shipping it would give every merchant the
# paid plans for free, and it is one of the things App Store review checks for.
# See app/lib/app-config.ts.
#
# SHOPIFY_BILLING_TEST=1


# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both default to the live IDs checked into app/lib/analytics.server.ts, so the
# trackers work with nothing set here. Point a deploy at a different property, or
# set either to the literal `off` to disable that tracker.
#
# GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=
#
# `shopify app dev` is excluded from tracking by default; set this to include it.
# Never leave it on — outside Electron, Clarity stores stylesheet *URLs* rather
# than contents, so anything recorded through a tunnel replays as unstyled HTML
# once that tunnel dies.
# ANALYTICS_IN_DEV=1


# ── Custom shop domains (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# SHOP_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=
